@*
    THE styling for operator-authored content-hub markdown (`.content-page`).

    ONE source, rendered by BOTH surfaces that show that markdown: the in-hub
    `/Info/{slug}` page and the anonymous public `/About`. It exists as a partial
    because the alternative had already failed — each page carried its own copy,
    the copies drifted, and §348's fixes (ruled tables, header background, zebra
    striping, heading spacing) landed on the in-hub page only. The PUBLIC page —
    the one the operator shares with people outside the event — kept the old
    thin-underline tables while its own comment claimed the two were identical.

    A page keeps only its own page-specific CSS (the photo/venue galleries, the
    About scroll wrapper); anything that styles the RENDERED MARKDOWN belongs here.
*@
<style>
    /* Mobile-first: keep floor-plan / feedback images inside the card on phones. */
    .content-page img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; margin: 8px 0; }

    /* §327a (operator 2026-07-25: "ceh intro - font is hard to read - maybe chg to same
       font but use italic or bold"). Inline `code` had NO styling at all, so it fell back to
       the browser's default monospace — noticeably smaller than the surrounding text and hard
       to read mid-sentence, which is exactly where the CEH intro uses it (HttpOnly, Secure,
       SameSite=None, frame-ancestors …). Keep the page's own font and mark the token with
       weight + a light tint instead. Real code BLOCKS stay monospace, below. */
    .content-page code {
        font-family: inherit;
        font-size: inherit;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #1e293b;
        background: #eef2f7;
        padding: 1px 5px;
        border-radius: 4px;
        white-space: nowrap;
    }
    /* A fenced block IS genuine code — alignment matters there, so it keeps monospace. */
    .content-page pre code {
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
        font-weight: 400;
        background: none;
        padding: 0;
        white-space: pre;
    }

    /* §348 (operator 2026-07-26: "it looks awful with the layout and it is very hard to read. if
       you want to use tables, then should the lines in the table"). Markdown tables had NO styling
       at all, so they rendered as unruled columns — no borders, no header separation, widths set by
       content alone, so rows ran together and the second column drifted far from the first. */
    .content-page table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        margin: 16px 0 28px;
        font-size: 14.5px;
        line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .content-page th,
    .content-page td {
        border: 1px solid #d7dee8;
        padding: 9px 12px;
        text-align: left;
        vertical-align: top;
    }
    .content-page th {
        background: #eef2f7;
        color: var(--el-darkblue);
        font-weight: 700;
    }
    /* Zebra striping: with long "what you get" cells, ruling alone is not enough to hold the eye
       on one row across the full width. */
    .content-page tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: #fafbfd; }
    .content-page td:first-child { min-width: 9.5em; }
    /* Wide tables scroll INSIDE the card on phones — never widen the page (mobile-first). */
    @@media (max-width: 700px) {
        .content-page table { display: block; overflow-x: auto; }
    }

    /* §348: headings butted straight against the preceding table ("8. Who built it" was crammed
       onto the row above). Space ABOVE a heading is what separates it from the previous section. */
    .content-page h2 { color: var(--el-darkblue); margin: 34px 0 10px; }
    .content-page h3 { color: var(--el-darkblue); margin: 26px 0 6px; }
    .content-page h2:first-child, .content-page h1 + h2 { margin-top: 12px; }
    .content-page p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
    .content-page ul, .content-page ol { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 22px; }
    .content-page li { margin: 3px 0; }
    .content-page hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb; margin: 28px 0; }
    .content-page blockquote {
        border-left: 4px solid var(--el-darkblue);
        margin: 12px 0; padding: 4px 14px; background: #f7f9fc; color: #374151;
    }
</style>
